    "date": "2014-11-10",
    "excerpt": "A’ashora is a happy event where we thank Allah for saving Mosa and the Sons of Israel from Pharos. However, most people associate it with mourning of Al Husain, may Allah be pleased with him. The Shi’a make this an event to express their grief and sorrow! They hit themselves with chains and knives [&hellip;]",
    "description": "A’ashora is a happy event where we thank Allah for saving Mosa and the Sons of Israel from Pharos. However, most people associate it with mourning of Al Husain, may Allah be pleased with him. The Shi’a make this an event to express their grief and sorrow! They hit themselves with chains and knives until they bleed in satanic marches that do not relate to Islam at all. The Shi’a belief is based on hatred and revenge. They are known of their deceit to Islam and Muslims. Throughout history, they have always helped the enemies of Islam against the Muslims. Their religion is based on Shirk, innovation and on giving a fixed percentage of their income to their leaders. Are they Kafir? The answer depends on the belief of the individual as we can’t paint them all with the same brush. By default, they are Muslims until proven otherwise. If one nullifies his Islam by slandering Mother Aisha or by cursing Abu Bakr and Umer, he is a kafir. If someone says that the Quran was changed or that they have a different Quran, he is Kufr. If someone believes that their Imams know the unseen or they call the dead, this is Shirk. May Allah guide them to Islam and to the Sunnah",
    "contentHtml": "<p><span class=\"userContent\" data-ft=\"{&quot;tn&quot;:&quot;K&quot;}\">  </span></p>\n<p><span class=\"userContent\" data-ft=\"{&quot;tn&quot;:&quot;K&quot;}\">A’ashora is a happy event where we thank Allah for saving Mosa and the Sons of Israel from Pharos. However, most people associate it with mourning of Al Husain, may Allah be pleased with him. The Shi’a make this an event to express their grief and sorrow! They hit themselves with chains and knives until they bleed in satanic marches that do not relate to Islam at all. The Shi’a belief is based on <span class=\"text_exposed_show\">hatred and revenge. They are known of their deceit to Islam and Muslims. Throughout history, they have always helped the enemies of Islam against the Muslims. Their religion is based on Shirk, innovation and on giving a fixed percentage of their income to their leaders. Are they Kafir? The answer depends on the belief of the individual as we can’t paint them all with the same brush. By default, they are Muslims until proven otherwise. If one nullifies his Islam by slandering Mother Aisha or by cursing Abu Bakr and Umer, he is a kafir. If someone says that the Quran was changed or that they have a different Quran, he is Kufr. If someone believes that their Imams know the unseen or they call the dead, this is Shirk. May Allah guide them to Islam and to the Sunnah</span></span></p>\n",
